From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: allow D3 on the SM8650 root ports

The SM8650 root ports (17cb:0113) set HotPlug+ in SltCap. With
CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE off, pci_bridge_d3_possible() then refuses D3, so
the ports stay in D0 across system sleep, dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() never
powers the links down, and the Wi-Fi and Renesas xHCI links keep their
interconnect and power votes (no CX collapse). Allow D3 on these root
ports. Same fix as the SM8550 set (0534). On the KONKR Pocket FIT the
Renesas link only survives this together with the PCIe suspend OPP on
both controllers (0013, 0014) and the Renesas firmware reload (0016).
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2427,6 +2427,19 @@
 	{ }
 };
 
+/*
+ * The Qualcomm root ports advertise HotPlug+ in SltCap, so the PCI core treats
+ * them as hotplug bridges and, without native pciehp, refuses D3 for them.
+ * Their links then stay up in system sleep and keep CX and DDR votes. Nothing
+ * is ever hotplugged on these boards, so allow D3.
+ */
+static void qcom_fixup_bridge_d3(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	if (pci_pcie_type(dev) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+		dev->bridge_d3 = 1;
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0113, qcom_fixup_bridge_d3);
+
 static void qcom_fixup_class(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
 	dev->class = PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI_NORMAL;
